    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm running a commercial organic kale operation up in the PNW and i noticed some clear nitrogen deficiency in my latest crop. my soil pH is sitting at 6.2 right now and i just put down some compost a few weeks ago. i'm looking to boost the nitrogen levels but i dont want to spike the pH too much. between bone meal and blood meal, which one would you recommend for this? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Between bone meal and blood meal, blood meal is a quicker source of nitrogen and would be beneficial for immediate needs in your nitrogen deficient kale crop. Bone meal swings the pH slightly upwards due to its calcium content, which you want to avoid. Additionally, using blood meal should help you condition the soil without dramatically impacting the pH. Consider applying blood meal at the recommended rate to maximize uptake while monitoring soil pH periodically.",
      "source": "target",
